## Critical Rules

### 1. Always Use ThemedText

`ThemedText` (`@/components/ThemedText`) is a `Text` with `text-primary` applied. Use it for all copy.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import ThemedText from '@/components/ThemedText';
<ThemedText className="text-lg font-bold">Title</ThemedText>
<ThemedText className="text-sm text-subtext">Muted caption</ThemedText>

// ❌ WRONG
<Text style={{ color: '#000' }}>Title</Text>
```

**Exceptions** (as in the codebase): white text on the `highlight` blue badge / `bg-sky-500` buttons (`subscription.tsx`), and inverted text on `bg-text` pills uses `ThemedText className="!text-invert"` (`BotSwitch`, `welcome.tsx`). The transparent `Header` variant renders its own white title.

### 2. Theme Colors Only — No Hardcoded Colors

Use the theme classes: `bg-background`, `bg-secondary`, `text-primary`, `text-subtext`, `text-invert`, `border-border`, `bg-highlight`, `bg-darker`.

- Icons: no `color` prop by default — `Icon` falls back to `colors.text`
- `highlight` (`#0EA5E9` sky blue) only for active states, badges and CTAs
- Changing the theme means editing **two files that must stay in sync**:
  1. `utils/color-theme.ts` — NativeWind `vars()` for Tailwind classes
  2. `app/contexts/ThemeColors.tsx` — JS values returned by `useThemeColors()`
- Default theme is **dark** (`useState<"light" | "dark">("dark")` in `app/contexts/ThemeContext.tsx`); `ThemeToggle` flips it via `toggleTheme()` + `colorScheme.set()`

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
<View className="bg-secondary border border-border rounded-3xl p-global">
const colors = useThemeColors(); <Icon name="Send" color={colors.invert} />

// ❌ WRONG
<View style={{ backgroundColor: '#323232' }}>
```

Deliberate fixed-color exceptions already in the code: the `AiCircle` gradient (`#D883E4 → #016BF0 → #3DE3E0 → #E57DDF`), `VoiceSelectCard` gradient (`#FD984D → #F77B79 → #F265D6`), the liked-heart pink `#E57DDF` in `Conversation`.

