### 4. Screen Layout Pattern

Nested screen (from `app/screens/profile.tsx`, trimmed):

```typescript
import { View } from 'react-native';
import Header from '@/components/Header';
import ThemedText from '@/components/ThemedText';
import Avatar from '@/components/Avatar';
import ListLink from '@/components/ListLink';
import AnimatedView from '@/components/AnimatedView';
import ThemedScroller from '@/components/ThemeScroller';
import { shadowPresets } from '@/utils/useShadow';

export default function ProfileScreen() {
  return (
    <AnimatedView className="flex-1 bg-background" animation="fadeIn" duration={350}>
      <Header showBackButton title="Profile" />
      <ThemedScroller className="!px-10">
        <View className="px-6 py-10 w-full border border-border rounded-3xl mb-4 items-center">
          <Avatar src={require('@/assets/img/thomino.jpg')} size="xl" />
          <ThemedText className="text-2xl font-bold mt-3">John Doe</ThemedText>
          <ThemedText className="text-sm text-subtext">johndoe@gmail.com</ThemedText>
        </View>
        <View style={shadowPresets.medium} className="bg-secondary rounded-3xl">
          <ListLink className="px-5" hasBorder title="Settings" icon="Settings" href="/screens/edit-profile" />
          <ListLink className="px-5" title="Help" icon="HelpCircle" href="/screens/help" />
        </View>
      </ThemedScroller>
    </AnimatedView>
  );
}
```

Chat screen (all four `(drawer)` screens follow this exact shell — copy `app/(drawer)/index.tsx`):

```typescript
<View className="flex-1 bg-background relative">
  <LinearGradient style={{ flex: 1, width: '100%' }} colors={['transparent', 'transparent', colors.gradient]} start={{ x: 0, y: 0 }} end={{ x: 0, y: 1 }}>
    <View style={{ flex: 1 }}>
      <Header title="" variant="transparent" leftComponent={[<DrawerButton key="d" />]} rightComponents={[<BotSwitch key="b" />]} />
      {hasMessages ? <Conversation messages={messages} isTyping={isTyping} /> : /* idle state */}
      <ChatInput onSendMessage={handleSendMessage} />
    </View>
  </LinearGradient>
</View>
```

- `ThemedScroller` already applies `px-global` and appends a `h-20` spacer — do not add horizontal padding to its children; override with `!px-…` or `px-0` as the screens do.
- `ChatInput` is `absolute bottom-0` and moves with the keyboard; `Conversation` pads its content by `insets.bottom + 140` so messages clear it.
- Screens without `Header` (login, signup, welcome, search-form, subscription) apply `paddingTop: insets.top` themselves via `useSafeAreaInsets()`.

### 5. Navigation

- Root `app/_layout.tsx` declares only `<Stack.Screen name="(drawer)" />`; every file under `app/screens/` is auto-registered as a stack screen (`headerShown: false` from `useThemedNavigation().screenOptions`).
- The drawer (`app/(drawer)/_layout.tsx`) registers `index` explicitly; the other three chat files are picked up by the file system. Links live in `components/CustomDrawerContent.tsx` (`History` array + `NavItem`s) — add a new chat layout there.
- Open the drawer with `DrawerButton` (dispatches `DrawerActions.openDrawer()`) or `useDrawer()` from `@/app/contexts/DrawerContext`.
- Paths as used in the code: `router.push('/screens/profile')`, `href="/screens/help"`, `href="/(drawer)/lottie"`, `router.push('/(drawer)/')` for home, `router.dismiss()` on the subscription modal. `Button`, `Icon`, `Chip`, `ListLink`, `Avatar` all accept `href`.
- New pushed screen: create `app/screens/my-screen.tsx` (kebab-case) with `Header showBackButton`; nothing to register.

### 6. LinearGradient Requires Inline Styles

NativeWind classes do not style `expo-linear-gradient` — pass `style={{ ... }}` (see `ChatInput`, `AiCircle`, chat shells). Children inside can use `className` normally.

### 7. Shadows

Use `shadowPresets.small | medium | large | card` from `@/utils/useShadow` (`ChatInput` card, `Conversation` bubbles, `profile` list). `getShadow(options)` is a plain function and is safe at module scope; never hand-roll `shadowColor/elevation` objects. `useShadow` remains as a deprecated alias.

### 8. Bottom Sheets

Wrap `react-native-actions-sheet` with `ActionSheetThemed` and a `useRef<ActionSheetRef>()` — `BotSwitch` is the reference. `Select` and `subscription.tsx` still use raw `ActionSheet`; do not copy that pattern into new code.

### 9. Inline Sub-Components

Repeated JSX in a screen becomes a small component at the bottom of that file: `TipCard` in `(drawer)/index.tsx`, `SuggestionCard` in `suggestions.tsx`, `RowItem`/`SelectPlan` in `subscription.tsx`, `RatingProgress` in `provider.tsx`, `UserMessage`/`AssistantMessage`/`TypingIndicator` in `Conversation.tsx`.

### 10. Status Bar / Navigation Bar

`useThemedNavigation()` (root layout) renders the themed `StatusBar` and sets the Android navigation bar style. Screens do not mount their own `StatusBar`.

