## AI Chat Logic

- `services/ai.ts` picks the provider from `EXPO_PUBLIC_AI_PROVIDER` (`openai` default | `gemini` | `claude`); `isConfigured()` returns false when the key is missing or still the `.env.example` placeholder, and screens then push a canned assistant reply.
- Each provider implements `sendMessage(messages)` and `streamMessage(messages, onChunk)`. Streaming is **simulated**: the full reply is fetched, then split by words and emitted every 30 ms. Real SSE streaming is not implemented.
- Conversation history is rebuilt from `messages` state on every send (`AIMessage[]` with `role: 'user' | 'assistant'`); there is no system prompt (README shows where to add one).
- `Conversation` renders assistant text with `Markdown` (styles built from `useThemeColors()`), shows `ShimmerText "Typing..."` while `isStreaming`, and like/copy/share icons once done (like state only; copy/share are not wired).
- `BotSwitch` (ChatGPT / Claude / Gemini sheet) is UI state only — it does not change the provider; that comes from `.env`.
- `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` keys are bundled into the client. Fine for a template/demo; note it if the user plans to ship.

## Voice Input

- `hooks/useRecording.ts`: `useAudioRecorder(RecordingPresets.HIGH_QUALITY)` from `expo-audio`, `startRecording()` / `stopRecording()` → file uri → `transcribeAudio()` posts `multipart/form-data` to `https://api.openai.com/v1/audio/transcriptions` (`whisper-1`). Without an OpenAI key it waits 1.5 s and returns a demo string.
- `ChatInput` drives it: mic/AudioLines buttons start, the "Done" pill stops; the `waves.json` Lottie overlays the input while recording, `ShimmerText "Transcribing..."` while waiting. Microphone permission strings are in `app.json` (`NSMicrophoneUsageDescription`, `RECORD_AUDIO`).
- `ai-voice.tsx` (voice picker) and `AiCircle`/`Sphere` toggles are visual only — no TTS exists.

## Mock Data

There is no `data/` folder; mock content is inline per screen: `aiModels` in `app/screens/search-form.tsx` (logos `assets/img/logo-1..5.png`), `faqData`/`contactInfo` in `help.tsx`, `slides` in `welcome.tsx` (Lottie sources), `History` links in `components/CustomDrawerContent.tsx`, `modelOptions` in `BotSwitch.tsx`, the six voices in `ai-voice.tsx`. Profile avatar is `assets/img/thomino.jpg`; `DrawerButton` `isAvatar` uses a `mighty.tools/mockmind-api` URL. The only network calls are the AI provider / Whisper endpoints.

