## Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Components | PascalCase, file = component | `CardScroller.tsx`, `ChatInput.tsx` |
| Themed wrappers | file `Theme*.tsx`, export `Themed*` | `ThemeScroller.tsx` → `ThemedScroller` |
| Screens | kebab-case | `edit-profile.tsx`, `mic-animation.tsx` |
| Route groups | parentheses | `app/(drawer)/` |
| Hooks | camelCase with `use` | `useRecording`, `useThemeColors` |
| Contexts | PascalCase + Context | `DrawerContext.tsx` |
| Services | camelCase files, named exports | `services/providers/openai.ts` → `openaiProvider` |
| Env vars | `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` | `EXPO_PUBLIC_AI_PROVIDER` |

## Testing Checklist

1. [ ] `npx tsc --noEmit` passes
2. [ ] Works in dark mode (default) and light mode (toggle in the drawer)
3. [ ] Uses ThemedText / theme classes (no stray hex values)
4. [ ] Uses existing components; horizontal scrolling via `CardScroller`
5. [ ] New pushed screens have a `Header` with `showBackButton`
6. [ ] Chat screens keep the `LinearGradient` shell, transparent `Header`, `Conversation` + `ChatInput` and clear the absolute input (`insets.bottom + 140`)
7. [ ] Works with and without an API key in `.env` (`isConfigured()` false path still renders a reply)
